<title>USA: Roberts Pharmaceutical Q1 turns to profit.</title>
<headline>Roberts Pharmaceutical Q1 turns to profit.</headline>
<dateline>EATONTOWN, N.J. 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>THREE MONTHS ENDED MARCH 31	     1997		1996</p>
<p>  Total Revenues			   $ 26.3		$17.2</p>
<p>  Gross profit				 14.7		  8.5</p>
<p>  Operating expenses			 13.3		 14.0</p>
<p>  Operating income (loss)		   1.4		(5.5)</p>
<p>  Income (loss) before taxes		2.3		(5.8)</p>
<p>  (Provision) benefit for taxes	 ( .7)		  1.6</p>
<p>  Net income (loss)			   1.6		(4.2)</p>
<p> Per share net income (loss)	     0.04	     (0.22)</p>
<p>  Wgtd avg shrs			30,681,000	 18,722,259</p>
<p>		  (in millions, except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: Full co name Roberts Pharmaceutical Corp.  </p>
<p>NOTE: Q1 1997 revenues do not include certain divested non-strategic product sales which were included in the 1996 figures.</p>
<p>Q1 1997 gross profit $14.7 million, up 73 percent from a $8.5 million a year ago. The gross profit margin expanded to 55.7% from 49.2% of sales, primarily reflecting product mix and the introduction of AGRYLIN.</p>
<p>On March 31, 1997, the Company's position of cash and marketable securities amounted to $94.1 million with long-term debt at $12.6 million.</p>
</text>
